        "problem": "$\\int ({sech}^{2}\u2061x-2\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x=$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x)=\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x & \\,\u21d2\\,\\int \\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x)={sech}^{2}\u2061x & \\,\u21d2\\,\\int {sech}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({sech}^{2}\u2061x-2\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {sech}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x+\\int (-2\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {sech}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}\u2061x-2\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
